    "answer": {
      "short": "$7.5\\text{ m}^2$\n\nUse the cosine rule to find an included angle, then apply the triangle area rule.",
      "worked": "Let $B=\\angle ABC$. Use the cosine rule, then the triangle area rule.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos B&=\\frac{5^2+3^2-6^2}{2(5)(3)}\\\\\\cos B&=-\\frac1{15}\\\\B&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac1{15}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac12(5)(3)\\sin\\left(\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac1{15}\\right)\\right)\\\\A&\\approx7.5\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the unrounded angle in the area calculation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
